edit('nsec-vpns','Transport mode (host to host):\n [IP][ESP][TCP|data][ESP trailer+ICV]\n       |-- encrypted --|\n\nTunnel mode (gateway to gateway):\n [new IP][ESP][IP|TCP|data][trailer+ICV]\n              |---- encrypted ----|','Transport mode:\n [IP][ESP hdr]{TCP|data|trailer}[ICV]\n\nTunnel mode:\n [new IP][ESP hdr]\n   {inner IP|TCP|data|trailer}[ICV]\n\n {braces} = encrypted portion','Explicitly delimit encryption; ESP header and ICV are not encrypted.',rfc(4303))
edit('nsec-vpns','**Tunnel mode** encrypts the entire original packet, including the inner addresses, and is what site-to-site VPNs use. **Transport mode** protects only the payload between two hosts.','For these confidentiality-enabled ESP examples, **tunnel mode** encrypts the original IP packet, including its inner addresses, and is suitable for site-to-site VPNs. **Transport mode** leaves the original IP header outside encryption. The ESP trailer is encrypted; the ESP header and authentication tag are not. Actual protection follows the negotiated algorithms.','Scope to confidentiality-enabled ESP and correct field boundaries.',rfc(4303))
